  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Amazon contribution to objective 1 of IOM&#x2019;s strategic plan: saving lives and protecting people on the move</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2026, the humanitarian system is facing unprecedented pressure, with over 240 million people in need of assistance and more than 83 million displaced globally (GHO 2026, GRID 2025). Conflicts, climate shocks, and socio-economic fragility are compounding vulnerabilities and triggering new waves of displacement at a scale never seen before. These crises are increasingly complex and protracted, exacerbated by rapid urbanization, inequality, and protection risks&#x2014;including gender-based violence&#x2014;leaving humanitarian actors struggling to keep pace.Under this project, IOM is establishing a fund contribution to its Global Response Mechanisms, specific to seed funding to IOM country missions to scale-up emergency preparedness and response capacities worldwide. By unlocking seed funding within hours, the mechanism will enable IOM country offices to launch life-saving operations, support national response systems, and build trust with partners and affected communities &#x2013; well ahead of traditional funding cycles.</narrative>
  </description>
